    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I did\n\nAdded a duplicate-telephone rejection to `POST /api/owners` that responds **409**, keeping structural impact low by adding small new units rather than growing existing functions.\n\n**New files (each a small, isolated unit \u2014 no surrounding class complexity to hold):**\n- `EnsureUniqueTelephone.java` \u2014 a pipeline step that scans owners and throws when the normalized telephone already exists.\n- `DuplicateTelephoneException.java` \u2014 a checked exception (per the escalation convention).\n- `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 Conflict`.\n- `...DuplicateTelephoneException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**One edit:** inserted the `ensureUniqueTelephone` step into `owners.POST.yml`, placed **after** `normalizeTelephone` so the uniqueness check runs on the normalized 10-digit value (and re-normalizes stored numbers defensively when comparing).\n\nThe check compares against the normalized digits of every existing owner, so `NormalizeTelephone` and the new step compose cleanly, and no existing function or class grew.",
